! be_sic_interrupt_entry.strap -- how MCP is entered: a BE into an
! IF-protected word, and an interruption table entry of SIC / BD.
!
! WHY IT EXISTS, AND WHO ASKED FOR IT.  MCP's IPL ends (printed p.34
! lines 23-31 and 44) by filling word 32 with a trap, fencing it with
! the boundaries (printed p.36 lines 39-40), turning IF's mask on and
! executing "BE,32.0" DISABLED.  MCP's interruption table entry for IF
! is "SIC,STIC" / "BD,SIFAE" (printed p.111 lines 2-3), and its IF
! analyzer reads the word at the stored counter -.32 for a B,$MCP
! (printed p.117 line 11).  The model got three things wrong in a row,
! each found by the run reaching the next:
!
!   1. It judged BE's TARGET with the enable state from BEFORE the BE.
!      Reference Manual printed p.40: BRANCH ENABLED "enables the
!      interruption mechanism, and then performs the same operation as
!      BRANCH"; monitoring is "ineffective" only while disabled
!      (printed p.32).  So the branch went through, the trap ran, and
!      MCP typed TYPE 16, "a successful branch to location 32.0"
!      (C22-6678-1 printed p.54).
!   2. A SIC whose branch half is BD took the branch and dropped the
!      DISABLE -- "STORE INSTRUCTION COUNTER IF BRANCH DISABLED" is
!      printed p.49's interruption-table instruction.  MCP's IF
!      analyzer then ran enabled.
!   3. That SIC stored the TABLE WORD's fall-through, not the
!      instruction counter, which "is not stepped during execution of
!      either interruption instruction" (printed p.48).  MCP typed
!      TYPE 1, "an IF interrupt, and the contents of the instruction
!      counter -.32 is not a B,$MCP".
!
! WHAT EACH CHECK ESTABLISHES
!   PC=PASS    the BE was suppressed (TRAP's B,BAD did not run) and the
!              interruption reached HANDLER.
!   saved_ic   SAVE's address field holds RET -- CALL+.32, the half-word
!              after the BE -- the counter MCP reads -.32 from.
!   entries    HANDLER ran ONCE.  It turns IF back on with IF's mask at
!              one; that interrupts again only if the BD failed to
!              disable, and each entry adds .32 to $X5.
!
! INJECTIONS: measured, and tests/run_tests.sh records them beside its
! entry.

        SLC, (8)4100.0
START   BD,  $+.32                   ! run disabled, as IPL does
        LVI, $X13, TBL
        SV,  $X13, $IA
        LVI, $X13, TRAP
        SV,  $X13, $LB               ! lower boundary := TRAP
        LVI, $X13, TRAP+1.0
        SV,  $X13, $UB               ! upper boundary := TRAP+1.0
        BBZ, 3.57, $+1.0             ! control bit := 0: signal INSIDE
        BBZ, $IF,  $+1.0
        BB1, 12.21, $+1.0            ! IF's mask bit := ONE
        LVI, $X5, 0
CALL    BE,  TRAP                    ! disabled HERE; enabled by the BE
RET     B,   BAD                     ! the counter SIC must store

HANDLER V+I, $X5, .32                ! count the entries
        BB1, $IF,  $+1.0             ! IF on, mask on: interrupts only
        NOP                          !   if the BD did not disable
        NOP
        BBZ, $IF,  $+1.0
        SV,  $X5,  CNT
        B,   PASS
BAD     B,   $                       ! hang: the trap or RET ran
PASS    BEW, $
        CNOP

        SLC, (8)4400.0
TRAP    B,   BAD                     ! the protected word: never runs
        CNOP

        SLC, (8)4500.0
SAVE    B,   0                       ! SIC stores the counter here
        CNOP
CNT     DD(BU,64), 0

! The interruption table.  IF is indicator 21.
        SLC, (8)5000.0
TBL     DD(BU,64), 0
        SLC, (8)5025.0
        SIC, SAVE
        BD,  HANDLER
        END, START
